Looking at the graph, the wave repeats itself roughly every 3.14 units: successive peaks occur near x ≈ 0.79, 3.93, 7.07 (and troughs near x ≈ 2.36, 5.50), with upward zero-crossings at x ≈ 0, 3.14, 6.28. This spacing of ≈ 3.14 = π corresponds to an angular frequency of ω = 2 (an integer), i.e., the curve is y = 3 sin(2x).

The period is therefore T = 2π/ω = 2π/2 = π.

\boxed{\pi}
